  "_typography": "Each block declares the computed values that would be wrong if its stylesheet never shipped or its rule lost to a broader selector. Both of those happened and all four scripts stayed green, because a block that renders, counts and aligns can still be the wrong size. DECLARED HERE, NOT READ BACK FROM THE CSS: comparing a computed value to the rule that produced it proves only that the browser works. `source` records where each value came from. `expect` holds values asserted at every width; `expectAt` holds the ones that differ by width."
